      {
        "label": "Used anabolic-androgenic steroids at some point, gender by Region, Gender, Age and Year",
        "source": "The Swedish Council for Information on Alcohol and Other Drugs (CAN)",
        "updated": "2026-06-04T11:57:00Z",
        "note": [
          "Indicator definition: Percentage (%) of the population (18-84 years) that has used anabolic-androgenic steroids or growth hormones without a doctor's prescription life time use. The results should be interpreted with particular caution as the prevalence is low.CAN is responsible for the survey and data were collected in 2013, 2017, 2021 and 2025 regarding use and consequences among the Swedish population with respect to alcohol, drugs, doping, tobacco and gambling. The data was collected through a survey (postal or online survey) based on a nationally representative sample of the population. In total 15,511 persons participated in the survey 2013, 11,514 in 2017, 9,819 in 2021 and 9691 in 2025, which corresponded to a response rate of 59.1, 44,3, 36.8% and 36,4% respectively."
        ],
